(7010866, 1061260, 15511, '<td valign="top">This would also look good in Black and White.</td>', 'This would also look good in Black and White.', '2013-04-01 02:30:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010867, 1061707, 93565, '<td valign="top">Not a big fan of the aggressive vignette on this. You might also consider getting closer and lower to emphasize the tree even more and decrease the prominence of the tracks in the snow. You''ve done a great job pulling bark texture from a backlit scene though.</td>', 'Not a big fan of the aggressive vignette on this. You might also consider getting closer and lower to emphasize the tree even more and decrease the prominence of the tracks in the snow. You''ve done a great job pulling bark texture from a backlit scene though.', '2013-04-01 02:45:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010868, 1061874, 93565, '<td valign="top">Oh sweet minimalism!<br/>I''d like to see a bit more detail in the facility through the use of some HDR maybe BW, but I still like this. You''ll probably get killed in voting, but who cares.</td>', 'Oh sweet minimalism!I''d like to see a bit more detail in the facility through the use of some HDR maybe BW, but I still like this. You''ll probably get killed in voting, but who cares.', '2013-04-01 02:47:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010869, 1059855, 93565, '<td valign="top">Looks very Great-Plains-y. Which means it''s my type of scene. <br/>I especially like the contrast of the storm on the left and the blue sky on the right. Nicely seen.</td>', 'Looks very Great-Plains-y. Which means it''s my type of scene. I especially like the contrast of the storm on the left and the blue sky on the right. Nicely seen.', '2013-04-01 02:48:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010870, 1061925, 93565, '<td valign="top">Looks like you may have been moving a bit between your source files for your HDR. You can try doing a single frame HDR for scenes where shutter speed is necessary or when you don''t have a tripod. You can also increase the deghosting. Great texture and warmth in the sand.</td>', 'Looks like you may have been moving a bit between your source files for your HDR. You can try doing a single frame HDR for scenes where shutter speed is necessary or when you don''t have a tripod. You can also increase the deghosting. Great texture and warmth in the sand.', '2013-04-01 02:50:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010871, 1061365, 93565, '<td valign="top">The stone on the left really intrudes into an otherwise much more idyllic scene.</td>', 'The stone on the left really intrudes into an otherwise much more idyllic scene.', '2013-04-01 02:50:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010872, 1059840, 93565, '<td valign="top">The editing has smashed an otherwise interesting room full of incredible textures and depth.</td>', 'The editing has smashed an otherwise interesting room full of incredible textures and depth.', '2013-04-01 02:52:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010874, 1061376, 93565, '<td valign="top">Nice concept, the execution is decent. Reminiscent of a <a href="//strobist.blogspot.com/2007/07/very-harry-summer.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Strobist shot</a>.<br/> <br/>The boy model is not nearly so interested as the girl, and it''s a bit hard to light since his skintone is somewhat darker as well, which means she is a bit more exposed than he is.<br/> <br/>Still, I like the idea here.</td>', 'Nice concept, the execution is decent. Reminiscent of a Strobist shot. The boy model is not nearly so interested as the girl, and it''s a bit hard to light since his skintone is somewhat darker as well, which means she is a bit more exposed than he is. Still, I like the idea here.', '2013-04-01 02:59:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010875, 1061826, 93565, '<td valign="top">I assume you''re shooting through a window here. Either that or you have some other weird reflections getting into your shot. To help alleviate this, you can either use a polarizer or you can get very close to the glass, which can prevent the reflections from reaching the glass and ever causing you trouble. You''ve also got a good bit of noise going on here, so I recommend shooting at a lower ISO or being cautious in your editing.</td>', 'I assume you''re shooting through a window here. Either that or you have some other weird reflections getting into your shot. To help alleviate this, you can either use a polarizer or you can get very close to the glass, which can prevent the reflections from reaching the glass and ever causing you trouble. You''ve also got a good bit of noise going on here, so I recommend shooting at a lower ISO or being cautious in your editing.', '2013-04-01 03:02:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010876, 1061248, 93565, '<td valign="top">I enjoy how all of the lines lead back into her face. Nicely done.</td>', 'I enjoy how all of the lines lead back into her face. Nicely done.', '2013-04-01 03:03:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010877, 1061808, 93565, '<td valign="top">The hardest thing about these shots is deciding if you want to make things properly level by using the trees or visually level by using the lake shore. This one FEELS really tipped, though I know it''s not. Sometimes, the shooting location needs to be changed to avoid such a feeling.</td>', 'The hardest thing about these shots is deciding if you want to make things properly level by using the trees or visually level by using the lake shore. This one FEELS really tipped, though I know it''s not. Sometimes, the shooting location needs to be changed to avoid such a feeling.', '2013-04-01 03:06:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010878, 1059924, 93565, '<td valign="top">I''m not really sure why I''m a sucker for foggy sheep shots, but I am. Interesting how decrepit the ewe on the right looks. Nicely done.</td>', 'I''m not really sure why I''m a sucker for foggy sheep shots, but I am. Interesting how decrepit the ewe on the right looks. Nicely done.', '2013-04-01 03:08:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010879, 1060734, 93565, '<td valign="top">Clean industrial shot. The water looks a bit grainy, but interesting cityscape.</td>', 'Clean industrial shot. The water looks a bit grainy, but interesting cityscape.', '2013-04-01 03:09:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010880, 1060180, 93565, '<td valign="top">Macro shots really require intense sharpness and a bit more depth of field than this affords.</td>', 'Macro shots really require intense sharpness and a bit more depth of field than this affords.', '2013-04-01 03:10:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010881, 1061815, 93565, '<td valign="top">Really like the light on her here- it works great with her skintone and hair color.</td>', 'Really like the light on her here- it works great with her skintone and hair color.', '2013-04-01 03:13:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010887, 1061306, 70393, '<td valign="top">//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_vote_image.php?IMAGE_ID=1061306#</td>', '//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_vote_image.php?IMAGE_ID=1061306#', '2013-04-01 03:21:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010888, 1061213, 93565, '<td valign="top">Curious to see if there are any notes on this one afterward. It''s an interesting shot, but it certainly doesn''t make me think first of seduction. One of my higher votes- captures an intriguing moment.</td>', 'Curious to see if there are any notes on this one afterward. It''s an interesting shot, but it certainly doesn''t make me think first of seduction. One of my higher votes- captures an intriguing moment.', '2013-04-01 03:22:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(7010894, 1061933, 93565, '<td valign="top">I like negative space, and this has about as much negative as you can get. Personally, I might have looked at the shot horizontally, to emphasize the vastness of ocean they are facing instead of sky, but this is still cool.</td>', 'I like negative space, and this has about as much negative as you can get. Personally, I might have looked at the shot horizontally, to emphasize the vastness of ocean they are facing instead of sky, but this is still cool.', '2013-04-01 03:25:58.000000', NULL, 1),
